.TH ZERODDS-AMQP-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-amqp-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-amqp-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/amqp-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the AMQP 1.0 bridge daemon maps DDS topics onto
AMQP addresses. The schema is the one of
.IR zerodds-amqp-bridge-daemon-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the reader is
.I DaemonConfig::from_config
in
.IR crates/amqp-endpoint/src/bridge_daemon/config.rs .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR domain ", " log_level ", " amqp ", " acl ", " metrics ", " catalog ", " topics ", " tenants .
.PP
An unknown top-level key is
.I not
a parse error. The daemon logs a WARN line on stderr naming the key, then
starts; under
.B \-\-check\-config
it is an error. An unknown key inside a known section, or a value of the
wrong type, stops the start with file and line.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed, so the
broker password belongs in the environment, not in the file.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
.SS amqp
.TP
.B broker_url
.IR amqp:// " or " amqps://
URL of the broker, e.g.
.IR "amqp://localhost:5672" ;
ports 5672 and 5671 by default.
.I amqps://
needs
.B tls
enabled, and the other way round.
.TP
.B container_id
AMQP container identifier of this daemon; it also seeds the GUID prefix of
the daemon's DDS participant, so two daemons need two ids. Default
.IR zerodds\-bridge\-<host> ,
the host name with its dots as hyphens, at most 32 characters.
.TP
.B channel_max
Highest channel number the daemon offers in
.IR Open .
.TP
.B max_frame_size
Largest frame the daemon accepts, in bytes, at least 512; a larger message
travels as a multi-frame transfer.
.TP
.B idle_time_out_ms
Idle timeout in milliseconds, sent in
.IR Open ;
0 announces none. The daemon sends a heartbeat at half the broker's.
.TP
.B hostname
AMQP
.I Open
hostname (virtual host); the broker host when empty.
.TP
.B sasl
Sub-map with
.B mechanism
.RI ( PLAIN " | " SCRAM-SHA-256 " | " SCRAM-SHA-512 " | " EXTERNAL " | " ANONYMOUS " | " XOAUTH2 )
and the
.BR username " / " password
pair the mechanism needs (for XOAUTH2 the password is the bearer token).
PLAIN without TLS and ANONYMOUS are refused towards a broker that is not on
the loopback interface. The broker must offer the configured mechanism.
.TP
.B tls
Sub-map with
.B enabled
(boolean),
.B ca_file
(required: the trust anchor for the broker certificate), the client material
.BR cert_file " / " key_file
(EXTERNAL's identity),
.B verify_hostname
(only
.IR true )
and
.B alpn
(only
.IR [amqp] ).
.TP
.B reconnect
Sub-map with
.BR initial_delay_ms ", " max_delay_ms " and " factor
of the exponential back-off after a lost connection.
.TP
.B cbs
Sub-map of claims-based security (the AMQP CBS draft, as Azure Service Bus
uses it):
.B enabled
(boolean; with it the links wait until a shared access signature token for
each AMQP address was accepted on
.IR $cbs ),
.B key_name
and
.B secret
(the shared access key, shown as *** by
.BR \-\-check\-config ;
.B AMQP_CBS_SECRET
in the environment), and
.B ttl_s
(the lifetime of a token in seconds, 10 to 86400, default 3600; the tokens
are put again at four fifths of it). With
.B enabled
over TLS, SASL ANONYMOUS is allowed towards a broker that is not on the
loopback interface. A refused token ends the connection; the daemon
connects again after its back-off.
.SS acl
.TP
.B default_deny
Boolean: a topic no rule names is closed.
.TP
.B rules
List of maps with
.BR topic ", " read " and " write :
the subjects allowed DDS \(-> AMQP and AMQP \(-> DDS;
.I *
allows every subject. The subject of the bridge is its SASL user; with
EXTERNAL it is the subject DN of the certificate in
.B amqp.tls.cert_file
as an RFC 4514 string (for example
.IR "CN=bridge-a,O=Example" ),
and the certificate's fingerprint
.I mtls:<SHA-256 hex>
names it too. ANONYMOUS has no subject; only
.I *
admits it.
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Turns on the admin endpoint serving
.IR /metrics ", " /catalog " and " /healthz .
.I /catalog
lists the daemon's topics, then each tenant's with the field
.IR tenant .
.TP
.B listen
Admin listen address. Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:9094"
when
.B enabled
is true; each bridge daemon has its own port, so several run on one
host without a collision.
.TP
.B path
Only
.IR /metrics .
.SS catalog
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. The daemon sends the topic catalog (JSON: every topic with its
type, address and QoS) once per connection, settled, on a sender link of
its own. Default
.IR true .
A broker that refuses the address leaves the other links running.
.TP
.B address
AMQP address of the catalog. Default
.IR zerodds.bridge.<container_id>.catalog ,
which RabbitMQ 4 does not accept; give a
.I /queues/...
address there.
.SS topics (list)
.TP
.B dds_name
DDS topic name.
.TP
.B dds_type
DDS type name; default the topic name.
.TP
.B keyed
Boolean: the type has key fields (entity kind WithKey). Default
.IR false .
.TP
.B type_file
Path of a serialized COMPLETE TypeObject of
.BR dds_type ,
optional. For a keyed topic in the direction AMQP \(-> DDS the writer reads
the instance keys with it: a dispose or unregister message names its
instance by
.I dds:instance-handle
alone, and with the type the DDS marker carries the serialized key. In the
direction DDS \(-> AMQP the reader computes with it the KeyHash of a sample
whose writer leaves PID_KEY_HASH out (Cyclone DDS does), which becomes
.IR dds:instance-handle ,
and reads the key of a dispose from its serialized key; without it such a
sample, and such a dispose or unregister, goes out with the nil instance
handle, logged once per writer as
.IR key_hash_unavailable .
A file that does not hold a COMPLETE TypeObject of a type with a key stops
the start. On a topic that is not keyed the key is refused.
.TP
.B amqp_address
AMQP node address, e.g.
.IR "/queues/orders.events" .
.TP
.B direction
.IR in " | " out " | " bidir .
.I in
carries broker messages into DDS (a receiver link and a DataWriter),
.I out
carries DDS samples to the broker (a DataReader and a sender link),
.I bidir
both. Default
.IR bidir .
.TP
.B sender
Sub-map with
.B settled
(send settled, at-most-once),
.B durable
(terminus durability 0, 1, 2),
.B snd_settle_mode
(0, 1, 2) and
.B rcv_settle_mode
(0 first, 1 second), for both links of the topic. With 1 a broker that
settles second sends its outcome unsettled and the daemon settles after it;
on a receiving link the daemon sends its outcome unsettled and keeps the
delivery, counted against the credit, until the broker settles it.
.TP
.B receiver
Sub-map with
.BR credit ,
the link credit the daemon grants.
.TP
.B qos
Sub-map with
.B reliability
.RI ( reliable " | " best_effort ;
best effort sends settled),
.B durability
.RI ( volatile " | " transient_local " | " transient " | " persistent ;
anything but volatile sends durable messages) and
.B history
with
.B kind
.RI ( keep_last " | " keep_all )
and a
.B depth
for keep_last: how many samples of a sender wait while the broker grants no
credit. A durability other than volatile also asks the broker for a durable
node (terminus durability 1 on the target of the sender link; the source of
the receiver link stays 0) unless
.I sender.durable
is set.
.B deadline_ms
(milliseconds, optional) is the deadline period the DataReader requests and
the DataWriter offers; a rise of the reader's missed deadlines is logged
.RI ( deadline_missed )
and the next message of the topic carries the total as message annotation
.IR x-opt-zerodds-deadline-missed .
.B liveliness_lease_ms
(milliseconds, optional) is the lease of the DDS endpoints (automatic
liveliness).
.B partition
(a list of names, wildcards allowed) is the partition of the DataReader and
DataWriter; a message carries its writer's partition in
.IR dds:partition ,
and a received message whose
.I dds:partition
matches none of the topic's partitions is rejected
.RI ( amqp:precondition-failed ).
.SS tenants (list)
Optional. Each entry is a DomainParticipant of its own with a broker
connection of its own (multi-tenant, spec \(sc1.1).
.TP
.B name
The tenant's name, in the log field
.I tenant
and the metrics label
.IR tenant .
Two tenants of one name are refused, the second with its path
.RI ( tenants[i].name ),
file and line.
.TP
.B domain
Its DDS domain.
.TP
.B amqp
Sub-map with
.B container_id
(mandatory, unique among the daemon's participants; it seeds the GUID
prefix),
.B hostname
(the virtual host of its open),
.B sasl
with
.BR mechanism ,
.B username
and
.BR password ,
and
.B tls
with
.B cert_file
and
.BR key_file .
What the entry leaves out is taken from the daemon's
.BR amqp .
.TP
.B catalog
Sub-map with
.BR address ;
default the catalog address of the tenant's container id.
.TP
.B topics
The tenant's topics, mandatory, with the keys of
.BR "topics (list)" :
.BR dds_name ,
.BR dds_type ,
.BR keyed ,
.BR type_file ,
.BR amqp_address ,
.BR direction ,
.B sender
.RB ( settled ,
.BR durable ,
.BR snd_settle_mode ,
.BR rcv_settle_mode ),
.B receiver
.RB ( credit )
and
.B qos
.RB ( reliability ,
.BR durability ,
.B history
with
.B kind
and
.BR depth ,
.BR deadline_ms ,
.BR liveliness_lease_ms ,
.BR partition ).
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/amqp-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-amqp-bridged (1).
